Let $u=(1-i,2)$ and $v=(i,3+i)$ in $\mathbb{C}^2$. Find $u+v$ and
$(2+i)u$.

Solution:
\begin{align*}
u+v &= (1-i+i,\ 2+3+i) = (1,\ 5+i)\\[4pt]
(2+i)u &= \big((2+i)(1-i),\ (2+i)(2)\big)\\
&= \big(2-2i+i-i^2,\ 4+2i\big)\\
&= \big(2-i+1,\ 4+2i\big)\\
&= (3-i,\ 4+2i).
\end{align*}
\[
u+v = \boxed{(1,\ 5+i)}, \qquad (2+i)u = \boxed{(3-i,\ 4+2i)}
\]

