Let $A=\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\3&4\end{bmatrix}$ and
$B=\begin{bmatrix}0&-1\\2&1\end{bmatrix}$ in $M_{2,2}$. Find
$2A-3B$.

Solution:
\begin{align*}
2A &= \begin{bmatrix}2&4\\6&8\end{bmatrix}, \qquad
3B = \begin{bmatrix}0&-3\\6&3\end{bmatrix}\\[4pt]
2A-3B &= \begin{bmatrix}2&4\\6&8\end{bmatrix}-\begin{bmatrix}0&-3\\6&3\end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix}2&7\\0&5\end{bmatrix}.
\end{align*}
\[
2A-3B = \boxed{\begin{bmatrix}2&7\\0&5\end{bmatrix}}
\]

